==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Bondage CatNEO '''at level 10.

Evolves into '''Ultimate Bondage Cat''' when obtained from the [[Bondage Awakens!]] (may drop on the first stage but guaranteed on the second) and is at level 20.

==Strategy/Usage==
Don't use this cat unless you are willing to invest in his Talents, as even in True Form, he is a much weaker version of [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]]. This is due to his very low stats and range. In addition, this Cat lacks powerful [[Cat Combo|combos]], unlike the other purchasable [[:Category:Special Cats|Specials]].  He's practically useless against non-Red enemies, making him a weak unit in mixed stages like [[Technocracy]].

==='''True Form'''===
Ultimate Bondage Cat's health doubles along with gaining Warp immunity and a chance to survive a lethal strike. By the time this form is unlocked, however, Bondage's stats have long fallen behind the standards, making these improvements inconsequential.

==='''Talents'''===
Talents change everything. With HP Buff and [[Dodge Attack]], Ultimate Bondage Cat becomes almost invincible against hordes of [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies, due to the powerful combination of good health and dodge chance against them, combined with a low recharge. All other talents are pointless without these. Slow immunity is situational and should only be unlocked if a situation strictly requires it. Freeze chance can help when a strong Red frontliner is present, basically covering Bondage Cat's main weakness; a hard hitting foe who hopes to take him out before he can trigger a dodge.

Ultimate Bondage Cat's slow speed still holds him back though, making other options, especially the more reliable [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]], preferable in most situations. However, Ultimate Bondage Cat has some use late into the game, as the combination of his Dodge and Strong Against allows him to stand in the way of the mighty [[Poultrio]], forming an excellent Dodge meatshield combo with [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]] in Poultrio's stages.

==='''Orb'''===
Ultimate Bondage Cat relies on health more than damage, so Defense Up vs Red is better than Strong Effect Up vs Red, but it can be used if you want to improve Ultimate Bondage Cat's effective DPS. It can be brought up to nearly 7k with an S grade Strong vs Red Orb.

