==Trivia==
*Bondage Cat, [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dom Cat]], [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Ninja Cat]] and [[Zombie Cat (Special Cat)|Zombie Cat]] all had their Strong Against ability removed in [[Version 2.0 Update|Version 2.0]] and readded in [[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.7 Update|Version 2.0.7]].
*[[Version 4.0 Update|Version 4.0]] gave Ultimate Bondage Cat the Survive ability.
*Bondage Cat was among the units that were given [[Immune to Warp]] in [[Version 6.5 Update|Version 6.5]].
*This unit is one of the only 2 purchasable Special Cats whose health is increased in [[True Form]], the other being [[Actress Cat (Special Cat)|Beefcake Cat]].
*In The Battle Cats Unite!, his name is renamed to "Bound Cat" to make the console version more kid-friendly.
*In the Nintendo Switch port, its True Form is still available and can be played, albeit via save file editing.
**At some point, the unused True Form was granted the Immune to Warp ability.
*[[Version 15.6 Update|Version 15.6]] changed Ultimate Bondage Cat's description to say "transcend'''a'''nt" instead of "transcend'''e'''nt". Despite the change, transcendant is actually the mispelling.

